  "honest_limits": [
    "CLOSED 2026-11-23, same day: the generator-vs-oracle_train bucket -- the LARGEST in every cell -- was published here as unmeasured and has now been measured. Exposure is the same order as the held-out path (worst 1.16 percent of oracle-train elements). See GENERATOR_SIDE_PATH_NOW_MEASURED. An EFFECT size remains underivable until a generator exists on this substrate, so the direction of that path is characterised by exposure only.",
    "The rescored quantity is the oracle's fold-9 Spearman under the deployed configuration, NOT the per-stratum matched-n ceiling the null artifact reports. The matched-n sd is used only as a scale reference for reading a delta.",
    "Overlap is computed on hg38 coordinates as published. A mis-stated coordinate in the deposit would be invisible to this and to any check built on it.",
    "The cross-cell count is on element NAME with sequence identity verified on a 3,000-id sample, not on all 7,321 shared HepG2/K562 ids.",
    "Fold 10's exposure is reported from keys only. No activity was scored, so nothing here states what a fold-10 number would be.",
    "This measures the SPLIT, not the oracle. A clean split does not make a 0.46-0.50 Spearman oracle strong."
  ],
